A||||7||Archie||Does anyone still buy from IRM?||||5||
Z||000000||Archie||10-04-2001||02:31 PM||||IMHO, IRM has some neat products. The IMSA kits, The Integrated Rockers and some scoops come to mind.<P>At least 5 times a week I get EMails & phone calls from people looking for These IRM parts. Of course these people have seen my IMSA car and the Blue Chop Top car with the Integrates Rockers. I answer these requests by giving out the IRM phone number.<P>My Qestion is.... What have you bought from IRM lately and what did you think of it?<P>Thanks<P>Archie<BR> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||10-04-2001||03:00 PM||||As someone who has bought parts in the past, (Actually I bought parts from them back in the late 80's and recently about 2 years ago) My personal opinion is that IRM has some very nice parts. It seems that lately many have had problems contacting them to order parts.<BR>I know that Haze and My7Fiero's are both looking for the Indy scoop. Last time I ordered from them I was told they were only taking orders on Tuesdays and Thursdays. <BR>I have one of IRM's original catalog's. Lots of many useful parts at good prices. I am not sure what parts they are selling these days. I bought my shift kit and Indy scoop from them. They are the only place that has the DGP original IMSA body kits for the coupe, aero-nocthback and GT. They also use to sell a 16:1 steering rack. I've actually been contemplating getting the wrap-around IMSA spoiler for my car. I am sure their business would be a lot larger if they had a website or even an updated catalog. Rumor has it the owner had some health difficulties and had made the business a part-time thing. Do you know for sure what is going on with them?<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||10-04-2001||04:36 PM||||Yep, As Oreif said. I'm buying a Indy scoop from them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">              .              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">        <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners - <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> - Pennocks Wild Rides - <A HREF="http://clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000003||MrPBody||10-04-2001||09:01 PM||||I bought suspension bushings from them a couple of weeks ago.  Service wasn't fast, but the bushings did arrive.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||10-04-2001||10:25 PM||||i got an egr tube from them about 2 weeks ago. ordered it mon. or tue., got it friday. got an indy scoop and rocker panels from them a year or so ago and they took awhile, but they eventually came. i want a couple more indy scoops eventually. <P>indy scoop group purchase...somebody mix the deal.<P>just remembered, <P>archie, i know you've used the rocker panel scoops on a few cars. did you ever use the for oil filters or cut away any metal behind them for more flow/access to the engine area?<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 10-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Doni Hagan||10-05-2001||01:58 PM||||About a week ago, I received some solid fiberglass sail panels from IRM that were ordered in July. I had forgotten I ordered them. Barbara was friendly in explaining the delay (vendor problems, I guess.) I'll do business with them again but next time I'll try to make sure they have the parts in stock beforehand. I plan to get a glovebox and some suspension components from them and would hate to see them go under. <p>[This message has been edited by Doni Hagan (edited 10-05-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000006||lou_dias||10-05-2001||03:33 PM||||I've bought from them before.  A couple of years ago.  Holley scoop, K&N filter, front 1" sway bar, Dual exhaust, hi flo cat converter, those HD exhaust gaskets, front spoiler||||reg||1
Z||000007||fix||10-05-2001||05:25 PM||||Information about IRM is rather elusive.  I finally got their e-mail address a couple months ago and requested a catalog from them.  I got a response saying they sent it, but I never got it.  Otherwise I probably would have ordered some stuff by now.  ||||reg||1
